    "title": "Stuttgart Urban Vegetation Mapping",
    "summary": "Applied U-Net semantic segmentation and YOLOv11 object detection to map tall and flat vegetation from high-resolution aerial imagery of Stuttgart. The project compared RGB and RGB+NIR inputs, evaluated model performance, and tested generalization on out-of-distribution aerial imagery. Results showed that semantic segmentation was most effective for precise vegetation boundaries, while object detection was useful for approximate localization and counting.",
